Same sieve of Eratosthenes, the same per-run array (vec![1u8; limit + 1] is array.fill of the state array each run) and the same checksum. The reference's (limit as f64).sqrt() is an integer square root by a loop here (at most 1,733 steps for the run parameters, negligible). Every array store is range-checked and undo-logged: Mitochondria requests are atomic, the reference's max-perf profile has no overflow checks.
